{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the problem and submitted the mitigation. The submission returned status 200.\n\n**Root cause:** Postgres rejected the `otelu` role's password. `product-catalog`, `recommendation`, `product-reviews` and `accounting` all connect as that role with `otelp_7k9m2q4x`, so they got `password authentication failed`. The frontend then showed \"Product Not Found\" errors.\n\n**Fix:**\n- I reset the `otelu` password in Postgres with `ALTER USER otelu WITH PASSWORD 'otelp_7k9m2q4x'`.\n- I restarted `product-catalog`, because it kept failing even after the reset.\n\n**Check:** After the restart, Postgres logged no more auth failures, and `recommendation` and `frontend` logs showed no new password or error lines. I did not test a full end-user request.\n\nI did not find out why the password was wrong in the first place. The password change is only in the running database, so if Postgres is recreated from scratch the problem could come back."}}
